  "issue_number": 6516,
  "issue_title": "toJSONSchema emits a base64url pattern that accepts strings z.base64url() rejects",
  "issue_body": "### Problem\n\n`z.base64url()` and the JSON Schema it generates disagree about the same string:\n\n```ts\nz.base64url().safeParse(\"A\").success;              // false\nz.toJSONSchema(z.base64url()).pattern;             // \"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]*$\"  \u2014 matches \"A\"\n```\n\nUnpadded base64url encodes 3 bytes per 4 characters, so a length that leaves a remainder of 1 mod 4 carries no whole byte and no encoder can produce it. `regexes.base64` already rules this out; `regexes.base64url` does not.\n\n`isValidBase64URL()` catches it at parse time, so `parse()` is correct. But `$ZodBase64URL` assigns the loose regex to `def.pattern`, and that is what `toJSONSchema()` emits \u2014 so a consumer validating against the generated schema accepts input Zod itself rejects. That matters where the schema is handed to something else (tool calling, a gateway) and Zod re-validates afterwards.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nGive `base64url` the same split `base64` already has \u2014 a strict pattern for the schema, a dedicated validator for parsing:\n\n- `regexes.base64url` \u2192 `/^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4})*(?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{2,3})?$/`, mirroring `regexes.base64`. This is what lands in `def.pattern`.\n- a new `regexes.base64urlCharset` (`/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/`) for `isValidBase64URL()`.\n\nThe second part is load-bearing: `isValidBase64()` never runs its pattern (it checks `length % 4` and calls `atob`), but `isValidBase64URL()` does run its own against user input of any size, and a quantified group overflows the stack on a long subject \u2014 the existing `big base64 and base64url` test (10 MB) hits exactly that. The length rule is already enforced downstream, where the padded string reaches `isValidBase64()`.\n\n### Status\n\nI have this implemented on a branch, with `\"A\"` added to the existing invalid fixtures in `string.test.ts`. `check:semver`, `check:comments`, `biome check` and the full `packages/zod` suite (7835 tests) pass, and runtime parse behaviour is unchanged.\n\nThe change is here, ready to open as a PR: https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/compare/main...oleg6k:zod:fix/base64url-pattern\n\nPR creation is currently limited to collaborators, so I am filing this instead \u2014 happy to open the PR as soon as that lifts, or to hand over the diff if someone wants to land it directly.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-08-31T17:16:14Z",
